| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| "Push to web" / manual open claude.ai as first default | CDP via `team_dispatch(model=cdp/…)` (project_ask = escape) per skill |
| Default binder/consult to bare `project_ask` when `team_dispatch(model=cdp/…)` is available | Prefer `team_dispatch`; `project_ask` only for IF6 / satellite-direct escape (missions: `purpose=` on `team_dispatch`) |
| Transport advice without loading CDP skill | `Use the claude-ai-cdp-navigation skill` first |
| Claim `workspaces://` unreachable on web; or cite `.cursor/skills/…` as the skill-delivery path | Prefer `cortex://` packaging for speed; Claude-slug engage or **inline** non-slugs for skills |
| Lead stages RAG then “merges” into deliverable when MCP `rag` is available (life or code) | Executing agent owns MCP `rag`; mapped URI is priming only |
| `project_ask(op="abort")` from IDE because arc path changed | Poll **private bus lane** + paste into live converse; abort only with explicit operator auth (`session-abort-authorization_ulg.mdc`) |
| `active_work` empty ⇒ "CDP unreachable / arc dead" | Transport idle ≠ bus idle — operator-proxy commissions live on `agent_bus.request` thread |
| Re-poll aborted `execution_id` expecting reconnect | Dead id — warm submit same `holder` + `converse=true` for Cowork CSE; bus continuity = request thread |
| Blame poller retain when Opus self-stopped after a leg | Load `cdp-operator-proxy` inv 30; page `cse-stream-stop` if unauthorized |
| Copy CDP mechanics into this rule | Defer to skill SOT |
